creation	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-10-23T21:27:22.7074138Z Note: a multi-user installation is possible. See https://nix.dev/manual/nix/stable/installation/installing-binary.html#multi-user-installation
creation	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-10-23T21:27:22.7082220Z ^[[1;31mSwitching to the Multi-user Installer^[[0m
creation	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-10-23T21:27:22.7167328Z ^[[32mWelcome to the Multi-User Nix Installation
creation	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-10-23T21:27:22.7175481Z ^[[0m
creation	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-10-23T21:27:22.7176276Z This installation tool will set up your computer with the Nix package
creation	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-10-23T21:27:22.7176807Z manager. This will happen in a few stages:
creation	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-10-23T21:27:22.7177076Z 
creation	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-10-23T21:27:22.7177908Z 1. Make sure your computer doesn't already have Nix. If it does, I
creation	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-10-23T21:27:22.7178483Z    will show you instructions on how to clean up your old install.
creation	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-10-23T21:27:22.7178805Z 
creation	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-10-23T21:27:22.7179015Z 2. Show you what I am going to install and where. Then I will ask
creation	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-10-23T21:27:22.7179446Z    if you are ready to continue.
creation	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-10-23T21:27:22.7179684Z 
creation	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-10-23T21:27:22.7180127Z 3. Create the system users ^[[34m(uids [30001..30008])^[[0m and groups ^[[34m(gid 30000)^[[0m
creation	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-10-23T21:27:22.7180734Z    that the Nix daemon uses to run builds. To create system users
creation	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-10-23T21:27:22.7181238Z    in a different range, exit and run this tool again with
creation	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-10-23T21:27:22.7181637Z    NIX_FIRST_BUILD_UID set.
creation	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-10-23T21:27:22.7181822Z 
creation	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-10-23T21:27:22.7182008Z 4. Perform the basic installation of the Nix files daemon.
creation	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-10-23T21:27:22.7182305Z 
creation	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-10-23T21:27:22.7182530Z 5. Configure your shell to import special Nix Profile files, so you
creation	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-10-23T21:27:22.7182960Z    can use Nix.
creation	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-10-23T21:27:22.7183107Z 
creation	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-10-23T21:27:22.7183210Z 6. Start the Nix daemon.
creation	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-10-23T21:27:22.7183329Z 
creation	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-10-23T21:27:22.7183527Z ^[[32m^[[4;32mWould you like to see a more detailed list of what I will do?
creation	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-10-23T21:27:22.7183879Z ^[[0mNo TTY, assuming you would say yes :)
creation	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-10-23T21:27:22.7185953Z 
creation	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-10-23T21:27:22.7186040Z I will:
creation	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-10-23T21:27:22.7186289Z 
creation	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-10-23T21:27:22.7186473Z  - make sure your computer doesn't already have Nix files
creation	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-10-23T21:27:22.7186917Z    (if it does, I will tell you how to clean them up.)
creation	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-10-23T21:27:22.7187405Z  - create local users (see the list above for the users I'll make)
creation	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-10-23T21:27:22.7187973Z  - create a local group (nixbld)
creation	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-10-23T21:27:22.7188245Z  - install Nix in /nix
creation	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-10-23T21:27:22.7188487Z  - create a configuration file in /etc/nix
creation	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-10-23T21:27:22.7188780Z  - set up the "default profile" by creating some Nix-related files in
creation	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-10-23T21:27:22.7189055Z    /root
creation	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-10-23T21:27:22.7199469Z  - back up /etc/bash.bashrc to /etc/bash.bashrc.backup-before-nix
creation	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-10-23T21:27:22.7200078Z  - update /etc/bash.bashrc to include some Nix configuration
creation	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-10-23T21:27:22.7209413Z  - load and start a service (at /etc/systemd/system/nix-daemon.service
creation	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-10-23T21:27:22.7209980Z    and /etc/systemd/system/nix-daemon.socket) for nix-daemon
creation	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-10-23T21:27:22.7210196Z 
creation	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-10-23T21:27:22.7211267Z ^[[32m^[[4;32mReady to continue?
creation	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-10-23T21:27:22.7211702Z ^[[0mNo TTY, assuming you would say yes :)
creation	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-10-23T21:27:22.7227221Z 
creation	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-10-23T21:27:22.7227690Z ^[[34m---- let's talk about sudo -----------------------------------------------------
creation	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-10-23T21:27:22.7236578Z ^[[0mThis script is going to call sudo a lot. Normally, it would show you
creation	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-10-23T21:27:22.7237175Z exactly what commands it is running and why. However, the script is
creation	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-10-23T21:27:22.7237640Z run in a headless fashion, like this:
creation	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-10-23T21:27:22.7237862Z 
creation	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-10-23T21:27:22.7238034Z   $ curl -L https://nixos.org/nix/install | sh
creation	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-10-23T21:27:22.7238291Z 
creation	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-10-23T21:27:22.7238526Z or maybe in a CI pipeline. Because of that, I'm going to skip the
creation	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-10-23T21:27:22.7238984Z verbose output in the interest of brevity.
creation	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-10-23T21:27:22.7239249Z 
creation	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-10-23T21:27:22.7239357Z If you would like to
creation	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-10-23T21:27:22.7239647Z see the output, try like this:
creation	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-10-23T21:27:22.7239861Z 
creation	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-10-23T21:27:22.7240070Z   $ curl -L -o install-nix https://nixos.org/nix/install
creation	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-10-23T21:27:22.7240512Z   $ sh ./install-nix
creation	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-10-23T21:27:22.7240672Z 
creation	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-10-23T21:27:22.7240679Z 
creation	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-10-23T21:27:22.7240913Z ^[[32m~~> Checking for artifacts of previous installs
